{"episodes":{"188547":"There were numerous evening reports of hail and some wind damage.","188550":"There were several late night marine thunderstorm wind gusts.","189325":"An upper level trough moved across Texas and provided sufficient lift to generate thunderstorms over South Central Texas. Some of these storms produced large hail.","189389":"The day started sunny on the islands as a cold front approached from the northwest. Instability was enhanced, and the moisture associated with the front triggered scattered to numerous showers across most of Puerto Rico. Later in the day, as the frontal boundary crossed the region, showers became widespread and strong, with thunderstorm activity detected. Rainfall accumulations ranged from 2 to 5 inches over the eastern interior and just southwest of the San Juan metro area. A few rivers over north-central Puerto Rico reached flood stage, and flash flood warnings were issued. Reports due to small streams out of their banks flooding small bridges and roads were received.","189870":"A low-pressure system moving across the Florida Keys brought thunderstorms with gusty winds across the nearshore Atlantic waters on the evening of March 22nd and the morning of March 23rd.","190066":"A line of storms moved across south Texas producing one report of severe winds at the Southeast Texas State Fair.","190069":"A line of thunderstorms moved across the region producing high wind gusts along the coast.","190072":"A line of thunderstorms moved through southwest Louisiana producing isolated severe wind gusts.","190469":"Two distinct rounds of deep, convective organization passed through the Florida Keys as a large upper-level low pressure system slowly evolved over the northern Gulf of Mexico.  Scattered to numerous gale-force wind gusts were recorded by coastal weather instrumentation due to thunderstorm outflow."},"events":[{"begin":"2024-03-22T00:00Z","county":"Harris","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024